WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.304
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:08.735
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.035 --> 00:00:14.938
Unit nine: WH-Questions (what/where/when). Today you will ask for information with question words.

4
00:00:15.238 --> 00:00:17.913
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:21.867
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:23.346
What.

7
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.500
What means used to ask about a thing.

8
00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:28.234
What is your name?

9
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.200
Your turn. Say: What.

10
00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:34.847
What.

11
00:00:35.583 --> 00:00:36.364
Where.

12
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.617
Where means used to ask about a place.

13
00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:41.369
Where do you live?

14
00:00:41.983 --> 00:00:44.450
Your turn. Say: Where.

15
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.139
Where.

16
00:00:48.883 --> 00:00:49.583
When.

17
00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.850
When means used to ask about a time.

18
00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:54.881
When is the class?

19
00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:57.950
Your turn. Say: When.

20
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:01.511
When.

21
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:02.822
Who.

22
00:01:03.817 --> 00:01:06.014
Who means used to ask about a person.

23
00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:07.827
Who is your teacher?

24
00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:10.465
Your turn. Say: Who.

25
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.115
Who.

26
00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:15.654
Why.

27
00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.835
Why means used to ask for a reason.

28
00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:20.556
Why are you late?

29
00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:23.768
Your turn. Say: Why.

30
00:01:26.633 --> 00:01:27.542
Why.

31
00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:28.994
How.

32
00:01:29.983 --> 00:01:32.447
How means used to ask about the way or manner.

33
00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:34.632
How do you go to school?

34
00:01:35.217 --> 00:01:37.428
Your turn. Say: How.

35
00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.024
How.

36
00:01:41.783 --> 00:01:43.005
Question word.

37
00:01:44.017 --> 00:01:47.595
Question word means a word that starts a question for information.

38
00:01:48.183 --> 00:01:49.788
What is a question word.

39
00:01:50.383 --> 00:01:53.187
Your turn. Say: Question word.

40
00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.197
Question word.

41
00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.067
Information.

42
00:02:00.083 --> 00:02:03.232
Information means facts about someone or something.

43
00:02:03.817 --> 00:02:05.352
I need some information.

44
00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:08.579
Your turn. Say: Information.

45
00:02:11.433 --> 00:02:12.678
Information.

46
00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:17.338
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.183 --> 00:02:21.567
Visal, do you know any question words? Name two.

48
00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:33.085
Yes! What and where. We also have when, who, why and how. They are called WH-words, and how is the exception.

49
00:02:34.183 --> 00:02:35.301
How do we use them?

50
00:02:36.417 --> 00:02:44.911
We put the question word first, then the helping verb and subject: Where do you live? What is your name? When does the class start?

51
00:02:46.017 --> 00:02:47.180
How do we answer?

52
00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:59.090
Not with yes or no. We give information. Where do you live? I live in Phnom Penh. When is the class? At nine o'clock. Who is he? He is my teacher.

53
00:03:00.233 --> 00:03:01.815
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:08.098
Grammar focus: WH-questions: question word plus helping verb plus subject.

55
00:03:08.398 --> 00:03:09.550
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:11.332
Where do you live?

57
00:03:12.217 --> 00:03:13.404
What is your name?

58
00:03:14.317 --> 00:03:15.921
When does the class start?

59
00:03:16.867 --> 00:03:22.886
Start with a question word, then a helping verb and the subject. Answer with information, not yes or no.

60
00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:26.558
Be careful! Don't say: Where you live?

61
00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.989
Say: Where do you live?

62
00:03:30.289 --> 00:03:32.161
Add do after the question word.

63
00:03:32.967 --> 00:03:35.770
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:38.032
Ask and Find Out.

65
00:03:38.332 --> 00:03:40.680
What is your name, and where do you live?

66
00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:44.374
Who is your teacher, and when is your class?

67
00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:46.832
Why do you study English?

68
00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:49.252
How do you go to school?

69
00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:52.998
These question words help us to find information.

70
00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:58.287
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.604
blank is your birthday?

72
00:04:00.904 --> 00:04:03.710
A, When. B, Where. C, Who.

73
00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:08.802
The answer is A: When.

74
00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.265
blank do you live?

75
00:04:11.565 --> 00:04:14.707
A, Who. B, Where. C, Why.

76
00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:20.429
The answer is B: Where.

77
00:04:21.583 --> 00:04:23.513
'Because I like it' answers blank.

78
00:04:23.813 --> 00:04:26.689
A, Where. B, When. C, Why.

79
00:04:30.233 --> 00:04:32.326
The answer is C: Why.

80
00:04:33.483 --> 00:04:35.227
Which question is correct?

81
00:04:35.527 --> 00:04:39.703
A, Where you live?. B, Where do you live?. C, Where live you?.

82
00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:45.394
The answer is B: Where do you live?.

83
00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.314
According to the reading, what do question words help us find?

84
00:04:50.614 --> 00:04:53.989
A, information. B, money. C, homework.

85
00:04:57.533 --> 00:04:59.603
The answer is A: information.

86
00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.801
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.474
Write three WH-questions to ask a new friend.

88
00:05:16.283 --> 00:05:17.795
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:18.095 --> 00:05:30.302
What is your name? Where do you live? What do you like doing at the weekend? I start each question with a question word. Then I add do and the subject. My new friend can give me information in the answer.

90
00:05:30.602 --> 00:05:32.276
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:33.183 --> 00:05:41.072
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and wh-questions: question word plus helping verb plus subject.

92
00:05:41.372 --> 00:05:45.185
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

93
00:05:45.485 --> 00:05:48.068
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

94
00:05:48.368 --> 00:05:50.985
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

